// Change: new rule
// Title: Script Interpreter Spawning Credential Scanner - macOS
// Sigma ID: 822e6453-105c-4934-ae40-253ac188f5ff
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Ritika (IsThisRitika)
// Date: 2026-07-21 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1552, execution, collection, T1005, T1059.007
// Description: Detects a script interpreter process (like node.js or bun) spawning a known credential scanning
//   tool (e.g., trufflehog, gitleaks). This behavior is indicative of an attempt to find and steal
//   secrets, as seen in the "Shai-Hulud: The Second Coming" campaign.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate pre-commit hooks or CI/CD pipeline jobs that use a script to run a credential scanner as part of a security check.
// References:
//   - https://github.com/asyncapi/cli/blob/2efa4dff59bc3d3cecdf897ccf178f99b115d63d/bun_environment.js
//   - https://www.stepsecurity.io/blog/sha1-hulud-the-second-coming-zapier-ens-domains-and-other-prominent-npm-packages-compromised
//   - https://www.endorlabs.com/learn/shai-hulud-2-malware-campaign-targets-github-and-cloud-credentials-using-bun-runtime
//   - https://semgrep.dev/blog/2025/digging-for-secrets-sha1-hulud-the-second-coming-of-the-npm-worm/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/e5d5f82b333647a2022d905f68f116c449f50754/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_susp_script_interpretor_spawn_credential_scanner.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/node" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/bun") and ((FolderPath endswith "/trufflehog" or FolderPath endswith "/gitleaks") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "trufflehog" or ProcessCommandLine contains "gitleaks"))
